## 14. Agent Autonomy & Multi-Agent Awareness
- Default: medium/high autonomy for builds and tests needed to verify your work.
- Report what changed and why; include test evidence before claiming “fixed” or “passing.”
- You may be working in parallel with other agents (e.g., Warp/Droid, OpenClaw, Manus).
- Do not assume you are the only agent modifying files. Always read the latest file state from disk before editing.
- If you see a `.lock` file or a comment indicating another agent is working on a section, do not interfere.
